# Downloaded paper sources

Whenever you download a paper for research, keep its `.tex` (and any accompanying `.bbl` / macros needed to read it) in a dedicated subfolder of `research/`. Do not leave sources in the repo root or in `paper/`.

- Name the folder after the paper, lowercase and compact (e.g. `research/gl15/`, `research/tiede24/`, `research/rotac25/`)
- Prefer the author-year or arXiv identifier already used as the citation key
- Skip giant ancillary files (full `.bib` dumps, nested PDFs) unless they are needed to verify a claim
